      "name": "fennel bulb",
      "amount": "2 large",
      "notes": "thinly sliced"
    },
    {
      "name": "rest-meat",
      "amount": "1 cup",
      "notes": "diced, cooked lamb or beef"
    },
    {
      "name": "red onion",
      "amount": "1 medium",
      "notes": "finely chopped"
    },
    {
      "name": "red wine vinegar",
      "amount": "2 tablespoons"
    },
    {
      "name": "olive oil",
      "amount": "1 tablespoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "pomegranate molasses",
      "amount": "1 tablespoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "sumac",
      "amount": "1 teaspoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "salt",
      "amount": "1/2 teaspoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "black pepper",
      "amount": "1/4 teaspoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "fresh parsley",
      "amount": "1/4 cup",
      "notes": "chopped"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Combine the sliced fennel bulb and chopped red onion in a large bowl",
    "Add the diced rest-meat to the bowl and toss gently",
    "In a small bowl, whisk together the red wine vinegar, olive oil, pomegranate molasses, sumac, salt, and black pepper",
    "Pour the dressing over the fennel mixture and toss to combine",
    "Sprinkle the chopped fresh parsley over the top of the salad and toss again",
    "Cover the bowl with plastic wrap and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes to allow the flavors to meld",
    "Serve the kisir chilled, garnished with additional parsley if desired",
    "Traditionally, kisir is served as a side dish or used as a topping for Turkish bread or crackers"
